    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and it passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the age-band feature on the `POST /api/owners` create flow so that a request may include an ISO `birthDate` and the owner's response carries a derived `ageBand`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (the source of the generated DTOs):\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema.\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` (string: `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`): added a persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter, so the value survives a round-trip and `ageBand` can be recomputed on every `GET`.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`): added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb; the others are updated for consistency.\n\n4. **`AgeBand` helper** (`function/owner/AgeBand.java`): new pure function computing the band from completed years between `birthDate` and `registrationDate` \u2014 `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), returning `null` when no `birthDate` was supplied so the field is simply omitted.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`**: added a `@Mapping` expression that derives `ageBand` via `AgeBand.of(owner.getBirthDate(), owner.getRegistrationDate())`, mirroring how the other computed read-only fields (e.g. `membershipNumber`) are wired. `birthDate` itself maps automatically by name in both directions.\n\n**Design notes:** Because `ageBand` is computed against `registrationDate` (which the pipeline defaults/business-day-adjusts on create), both dates are persisted and the band is derived purely in the mapper at read time \u2014 matching the existing convention for derived fields rather than adding a persisted column or extra pipeline step. No `@RestController`/Spring MVC was introduced; the existing OfficeFloor pipeline for `owners.POST.yml` already binds and persists the request body, so no YAML changes were needed.\n\nThe acceptance test (`birthDate: 1990-01-01` \u2192 `ageBand: ADULT` against a 2026 registration date) and the full suite pass.",
