        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots into the codebase's existing idiom cleanly:\n\n- `AgeBand` mirrors the established pattern of pure derived-value helpers in `rest.function.owner` \u2014 `IdentityKey` and `CustomerCode` are both `final` classes with a private constructor and static methods, invoked from `OwnerMapper` via a `@Mapping` `expression`. Placing the band logic here (rather than inlining a ternary in the mapper, or as a `default` method like `hasEmail`) is the right unit: the computation is non-trivial branching, matching the precedent of the separate-class helpers over the one-liner `default` methods.\n- The `null`-when-absent contract is documented and consistent with how the spec wants `ageBand` simply omitted, and the Javadoc explains the registrationDate-relative computation clearly \u2014 in keeping with the thorough class-level docs on its siblings.\n- `Owner.birthDate` field/getter/setter placement mirrors `registrationDate` exactly, and the schema column is added consistently across all four DB dialects.\n- The OpenAPI `birthDate`/`ageBand` additions follow the surrounding description/`readOnly` style.\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class is becoming a catch-all, and a maintainer would find this natural."
